# Agentic OS Build Policy

## STATUS_ONLY_CONNECTOR_PROFILE_V1

This profile applies throughout the complete Agentic OS build unless the user explicitly overrides it.

For every connector integration pass:

- Work only inside /opt/vrn/mission-control/builds/agentic-os-v1 unless explicitly overridden.
- Do not restart services.
- Do not start dormant tools.
- Do not attach to tmux, agent sessions, terminals, or old sessions.
- Do not send prompts, commands, jobs, or tasks to target systems.
- Do not wake old sessions.
- Do not enable heartbeat loops.
- Do not read secret values.
- Do not read .env values.
- Do not read auth files.
- Do not expose API keys.
- Do not enable command execution.
- Do not redesign the cockpit layout.
- Status-only means: read health/status/state metadata only, sanitize output, expose it through a server-side reader + API route + adapter wrapper.
- Use the existing live-status UI machinery created for Hermes, FCC/OwlAlpha, and OpenClaw.
- If a source is unsafe or ambiguous, skip it and report why.

## Current connector sequence

1. Hermes — live status-only
2. FCC / OwlAlpha — live status-only
3. OpenClaw — live status-only
4. Obsidian Graphlink — next
5. Paperclip / n8n / AGY / Browser Agents — later, status-only first

## Explicit override required

Command execution, service mutation, tmux attach, session wake-up, secret reading, or layout redesign may only happen after explicit user approval.
